WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Hey explorers!

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:02.260
Dad here.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.420
Can two worlds help us draw?

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.300
Mercury, the closest planet to the Sun,
goes around

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.240
in about 88 Earth days.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.660
Far away Pluto is a dwarf planet.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.920
One trip takes about 248 Earth years.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.440
One Pluto year is about as long as the
United States has existed.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.340
Mercury makes over a thousand trips, while
Pluto

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.180
makes one.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.960
Now, let's draw a line between them in our
simple

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:33.380
model.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.400
Keep each line as they move.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.460
Watch the thread spread.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.280
Look at that beautiful pattern!

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.940
These lines are our drawing, not strings
in space.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.740
What do you notice?
